For every $M_e>0$ there is a weak solution $u$ of  egin{equation} \divg_g E=0,\qquad E=e(w) rac{
abla u}{w},\quad w=|du|_g, \qquad u|_S=-M_e,\quad u\longrightarrow0	ext{ at infinity}, \end{equation} where $E=0$ at $w=0$. It satisfies $-M_e\le u\le0$, $|u|+|du|_g=O(r^{-1})$, and is $C^{1, eta}$ locally up to $S$ and in compactified coordinates $(ho,\omega)$ up to $ho=0$, for some $ eta>0$, where $ho=e^{-\eta}$. The continuous symmetric tensor  egin{equation} \Pi=L(w)g-du\otimes E^ lat \end{equation} is distributionally divergence free, is positive definite, and obeys  egin{equation} (	r_g\Pi)^2-2|\Pi|_g^2=3. \end{equation} There is a continuous nonnegative function $e_0$ on $\Sph^2$ such that, uniformly in angle,  egin{equation} r^2|E|_g\longrightarrow e_0,\qquad r^3 ig(\Pi(
u,
u)-1 ig) \longrightarrow-	frac12 e_0^{3/2}. \end{equation} Here $
u$ points toward increasing $r$. The charge  egin{equation} F_{M_e}=\int_{r=R}g(E,
u)\,\dd A_g \end{equation} is independent of large $R$, satisfies $F_{M_e}\le\int_{\Sph^2}e_0\,\dd A_\sigma$, and  egin{equation} \liminf_{M_e	o\infty}F_{M_e}\ge A_*. \end{equation}
